# rauc — built FROM SOURCE at 1.15.2 via a novadeck-owned PKGBUILD (packages/rauc/PKGBUILD),
# NOT fetched from the holo monorepo. holo HAS a rauc recipe, but only at 1.14
# (holo-core-aarch64-preview extra-aarch64/r/rauc/1.14-1) — and 1.14 cannot install a dm-verity
# bundle on kernel >= 6.19, which is every kernel we ship. Our PKGBUILD IS that holo recipe with
# the version bumped to 1.15.2; see the header comment there for the two mechanical deviations.
#
# This is the "local PKGBUILD" form (like packages/gtk2, packages/mesa): build-overlay.sh sees
# `pkgbuild_local` and uses the checked-in recipe instead of curl'ing one from GitLab. makepkg
# still downloads the upstream release tarball the PKGBUILD names.
#
# Fields:
#   name           pkgname (must match the PKGBUILD); also the work/ build-dir + repo entry
#   pkgbuild_local path (relative to this dir) to the checked-in PKGBUILD to build
#   pkgrel_suffix  numeric suffix appended to the PKGBUILD's pkgrel (N -> N.<suffix>) so pacman
#                  prefers our build on later upgrades. Integer only (makepkg requires
#                  pkgrel = integer[.integer]). Belt-and-braces here: 1.15.2 already outranks
#                  holo's 1.14 by pkgver, so the suffix only matters if holo ever ships 1.15.2-1.
#
# No `patches:` — we carry zero novadeck patches against rauc; the whole point of this recipe is
# the upstream version, unmodified.
#
# To bump rauc: edit pkgver in packages/rauc/PKGBUILD, replace both checksums (sha512sum and
# b2sum of the new .tar.xz), and re-read upstream's meson_options.txt / NEWS for new dependencies
# — makepkg runs with --skipinteg, so a stale checksum will NOT fail the build, it will just be
# a lie in the recipe.
name: rauc
pkgbuild_local: PKGBUILD
pkgrel_suffix: 1
